cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Simuwire in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
title: "Simuwire: a browser-based block diagram simulator"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Gülgönül"
    given-names: "Şenol"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5346-4448"
version: "1.4.1"
date-released: "2026-10-26"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/senolgulgonul/simuwire"
url: "https://senolgulgonul.github.io/simuwire/"
abstract: >-
  Simuwire is a zero-install block diagram simulator that runs in the web
  browser. It provides a Simulink-style editor, a PID Controller block,
  transfer functions, transport delay, a hysteresis relay for on-off control and other basic blocks, fixed-step
  Runge-Kutta simulation, and import of Simulink .slx and .mdl files. It is
  intended for teaching introductory control systems.
keywords:
  - control systems
  - simulation
  - block diagram
  - PID control
  - engineering education
